  "title": "Mainsah et al. 2025 — bigP3BCI: An Open, Diverse and Machine Learning Ready P300-based Brain-Computer Interface Dataset (Study S2)",
  "description": "This dataset contains EEG recordings from 24 healthy participants in Study S2 of the bigP3BCI collection. Participants used a P300-based speller with a 9x8 grid and a house/tool stimulus paradigm. Data were recorded from 32 channels at 256 Hz and annotated with HED tags for target and non-target events. It is a MOABB-derived version of the PhysioNet bigP3BCI release.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded with a g.USBamp amplifier (g.tec) from 32 channels using a standard 10-20 montage at a 256 Hz sampling rate. Participants performed a P300 speller task on a 9x8 character grid with calibration followed by online testing with feedback. Events were labeled Target or NonTarget, with epochs spanning 0 to 1.0 s.",
